Two gaps in how the 10-second session-start sync ends. (1) Git terminal prompts are on; in a hook there is no terminal, so a remote that asks for a password waits until the deadline instead of failing at once. Set GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 for the hook sync only (git.Repo needs a per-caller way to add it); credential helpers, keychain, biometric and SSH agent prompts are unaffected by it. (2) internal/git sets no WaitDelay on its commands, so after the deadline kills git, a credential helper or ssh child still holding git output pipe keeps the hook waiting; set a WaitDelay of a second or two on every git command. Neither shortens the deadline: a user mid-auth at ten seconds is cut off by the deadline as designed, safely (nothing local is written before the push lands). (3) When the hook sync times out, the Last sync fact should add a hint: run tess sync to finish authenticating. Update sync.txtar and the README Hooks facts for the hint.